<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8380" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cirrha</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cirra</span></b> ), ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κίρρα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a very ancient town in Phocis</i>, <i>near Delphi</i>, devoted to Apollo, <i><span class="en">Liv. 42,
				15, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 3, 474</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 3,
			172</span></i>; Mart, 1, 77; cf. <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3,
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 3, 4, §
			7</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cirrhaeus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cirraeus</span></b> ), a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Cirrha</i>, or (in post-Aug. poets freq.) <i>to Apollo</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">campi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 4,
					3, 4, § 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">templa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Oet. 92</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cirrhaea vates,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of Delphi</i>, <i>Delphic</i>, <i>of the
						Pythia</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Oedip. 269</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 3, 106</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cirrhaeus vates,</span>”
				<i>of Apollo</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					13, 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antra,</span>”
				i.e. <i>the Delphic oracle</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Luc. 5,
					95</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sil.
				3, 9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hiatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 8, 331</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">secreta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc. 1,
					64</span></i>
			.</div>
